{title: Jesus Come}
{artist: Larry Holder / Elton Smith}
{time: 4/4}
{key: C}
{tempo: 83}

Verse 1
[C]All the world's in travail
[G]From [B]the [Am]hills to the [Em]sea
Sin and [F]death have their [G]way
So it seems.
[C]How we long for the day
[G]When the Word [Am]shall [Em]prevail
[Em7]When [G]the [F]Lord--- comes [G]again!

Chorus
[C]Jesus, come!
End the night
[Am]Fill the [E]world [Em]With Your [G]light
Be enthroned,
[C]Come and [Am]reign with no [G]end.
[Fmaj7]Let [C]the nations rejoice
[Fmaj7](Let the nations rejoice)
[C]To Your praise lift a voice
[F](To Your praise lift a voice)
Lord we long for [D7]the [G]day
You come again!

Verse 2
[C]All the world cries for [G]peace
Yet the [Am]wars linger [E]on
[Em]There's no [F]hope for a [G]change
So it [C]seems.
[C]Yet the promise [G]remains
For a [Am]new age to [A]dawn
[Em]When the [F]Lord--- comes again!
[C](Repeat Chorus)
[G]Jesus, come!
[C]End the [Am]night
Fill the [Em]world With Your [G]light
Be [C]enthroned,
Come and [A]reign [Am7]with no [G]end.
[C]Let the nations [F]rejoice
(Let the nations rejoice)
[C]To Your [C]praise lift a [F]voice
(To Your praise lift a voice)
Lord we long [F]for the [G]day
You come [C]again!

Ending
[D7]Bring Your [F]love
Bring Your peace
[Am]Bring Your [Em]joy
[C]Come again!
